error: `both` holds the thread until it is done, and an async function does not hold its thread
  the tasks of async functions share a few threads: one that holds its thread keeps the others from running
  --> error_async_waits_through_call.sg:11:11
 11 |     print(both())
    |           ^^^^
  `both` does `wait` here:
  --> error_async_waits_through_call.sg:7:17
 7 |     return task.wait()
   |                 ^^^^
  hint: a function that does it runs on a thread of its own with `await Task.run(work, x)`
